                  "endLine": 221,
                  "startLine": 207
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Restore verifies a different read from the archive it consumes and mutates before complete validation\n\nrestoreBackup verifies one decompression then decompresses again without validating that second object. Validation also accepts '.' and duplicate or file/parent-conflicting paths when their content checksums match. With force, target is deleted before extraction discovers such conflicts. Decompressed bytes are unbounded.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Data integrity\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-367\n\nRemediation:\nRead once with a decompressed-byte bound, validate strict entry shape and canonical unique nonconflicting file paths, stage the full store before replacement, then restore exactly the validated bytes."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:23c00bc303549f17ab73da4d0b1d5ac1e03135931f9b5c2c3a28692df735b3d6",
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "37baea43ff2f2556:1"
          },
          "properties": {
            "category": "data-integrity",
            "confidence": "high",
            "findingId": "csf_df99eca10f8103830a7fa6a5",
            "occurrenceId": "occ_93bbe81d356efcb65f1b0550",
            "severity": "medium"
          },
          "ruleId": "intake.sec-07",
          "ruleIndex": 6
        },
        {
          "level": "warning",
          "locations": [
            {
              "message": {
                "text": "root_control"
              },
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/policy.js"
                },
                "region": {
                  "endLine": 4,
                  "startLine": 4
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Nonmatching policies silently authorize through first-policy fallback\n\nA failed policies.find falls back to policies[0], even when that policy explicitly scopes itself to a different source/category.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Authorization\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-863\n\nRemediation:\nReturn a blocked result when no policy applies; preserve explicit wildcard behavior."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:89d5fc8017d60c8d8d3c4251b2f37f1683c96773de138056166a6ccba64e3561",
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "daaa892abc2cb577:1"
          },
          "properties": {
